# RimKit VSIX always current

When this session changes anything Lua authors see (host ops, OO bindings, infrastructure/docs/api, examples that introduce new `rim.*` / `anomaly.*` / `ui.*` / `pawn.*` / `game.*` surfaces), update the VS Code extension **before ending the turn**.

## Checklist (do all)

1. Update `src/editor/stubs/rimkit.lua` and completions in `src/editor/extension.js` for new/changed APIs.
2. Bump `src/editor/package.json` `version` (patch for API docs/completions; minor for extension behavior).
3. Repackage from `src/editor`:

```powershell
cd src/editor
npx --yes @vscode/vsce package --no-dependencies
```

4. Confirm `src/editor/rimkit-<version>.vsix` exists and matches the new version. Remove or leave stale `rimkit-*.vsix` only if README points at the latest.
5. If README / `infrastructure/docs/**` mention a VSIX path or version, update that path.

## Skip only when

- Change is host/native internals with **no** new Lua-facing name.
- Pure ship/allowlist/DLL copy with no API surface change.

## Install note

Do not require reinstall every time. Say: reload window or `cursor --install-extension .\src\editor\rimkit-<version>.vsix` if user needs fresh completions.
